# The Dockerfile ends in `COPY . .`, so anything not excluded here is baked
# into a published image layer. Image layers are permanent and world-readable
# on a public registry: deleting a file in a later layer does NOT remove it —
# `docker save` still recovers it. Treat this file as a publication boundary,
# not a build optimisation.

# --- Credentials: the reason this file exists -----------------------------
# `apps/api/.env` carries live OpenAI / Anthropic / TinyFish / Mailjet SMTP
# credentials. It is gitignored, which protects the repo and does nothing at
# all for a docker build — the build context reads the working directory, not
# git. `.env.example` is deliberately NOT excluded: it is placeholders only and
# documents every setting in core/config.py.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Local databases ------------------------------------------------------
# dev.db holds seeded users with a known password; test.db is suite residue.
# Neither belongs in an image, and a shipped SQLite file would also mask a
# missing DATABASE_URL by letting the app start against the wrong database.
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# --- Virtualenv -----------------------------------------------------------
# Built on Windows against python3.12 — the binaries cannot run in a Linux
# image, and the Dockerfile pip-installs from requirements.txt anyway. Copying
# it adds hundreds of megabytes of unusable weight.
.venv/
venv/

# --- Trained model artifacts ---------------------------------------------
# Gitignored and rebuilt by `python -m agents.<agent>.train`. Shipping a stale
# model silently would be worse than shipping none: the agents fall back to a
# transparent heuristic and say so, which a stale artifact would not.
agents/*/artifacts/
data/

# --- Build/test residue ---------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
tests/

# --- Editor / OS ----------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
